id: DRAFT-cloop-3.14.1.3-nmu1-ohos
trigger_tool: configure|clang|make|conan|test_package
phase: configure|build|testing
error_signature: >-
  sys/socketvar.h: file not found|
  invalid operands to binary expression .* __bind|
  unknown type name 'loff_t'|
  cannot create ./confstat.*: Permission denied|
  Operation not permitted.*ln -f
severity: 2
category: autotools|makefile|hmdfs|ohos|libcxx|portability
match_keywords: sys/socketvar.h, std::bind, ::bind, loff_t, int64_t, confstat, umask 077, HMDFS, ln -f, advancecomp
root_cause: >-
  cloop bundles an old advancecomp Autotools tree and Linux-oriented C/C++ utilities.
  HarmonyOS lacks sys/socketvar.h and Linux loff_t in the OHOS sysroot; libc++ exposes
  std::bind so an unqualified POSIX bind call resolves incorrectly; HMDFS preserves
  the restrictive umask used by generated configure scripts and rejects hard-link
  replacement. The kernel module is also outside the HarmonyOS PC user-space scope.
affected_scope: >-
  Legacy Autotools or Makefile packages that bundle generated configure scripts,
  use Linux-only compatibility headers/types, or install with ln -f on HMDFS.
verification_cmd: >-
  configure with explicit aarch64 build/host; build user-space tools with clang -j1;
  run create_compressed_fs and extract_compressed_fs on an 8192-byte input;
  verify the original prefix and zero block padding.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: >-
  Keep the kernel module out of the OHOS PC package. Pass explicit build/host values,
  patch generated configure umask to 022, guard the optional socketvar include with
  __has_include, qualify ::bind, replace loff_t with int64_t, and copy rather than
  hard-link the compressor executable.
rec_description: >-
  These changes are source-compatible portability fixes and preserve the cloop image
  header and 64-bit offset representation. The consumer test exercises the packaged
  tools as a real downstream rather than only checking file existence.
rec_auto_fix: false
status: draft
